  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                                                                                
                      Program APOST-3D, Version 4                               
                               12-03-2025                                       
                     --------------------------------                           
                                                                                
      Real-space and Hilbert-space tools for wave function analysis             
                                                                                
      Available atomic definitions:                                             
      ----------------------------                                              
                                                                                
      Real space:                                                               
        Becke, J. Chem. Phys. 88 2547 1988                                      
        Hirshfeld, Theor. Chim. Acta 44  129 1977                               
        Hirshfeld-Iterative, J Chem Phys 126 144111 2007                        
        Topological fuzzy Voronoi cells (TFVC), J Chem Phys 139 071103 2013     
        QTAIM, J. Comput. Chem 30 1082 2009                                     
                                                                                
      Hilbert-space : Mulliken, Lowdin, Davidson-Lowdin                         
                                                                                
                                                                                
      Calculating:                                                              
      ------------                                                              
                                                                                
        A) Atomic and overlap populations, bond orders and valences             
           I. Mayer and P. Salvador, Chem. Phys. Lett. 383 368-375 2004	        
                                                                                
        B) Hartree-Fock molecular energy decomposition                          
           P. Salvador, M. Duran, I.Mayer, J. Chem. Phys. 115 1153-1157 2001    
           P. Salvador and I. Mayer, J. Chem. Phys. 120 5046-5052 2004          
                                                                                
        C) KS-DFT molecular energy decomposition                                
            P. Salvador, I. Mayer, J. Chem. Phys. 126 234113 2007	              
           M. Gimferrer, P. Salvador, J. Chem. Phys. 158 234105 2023            
                                                                                
        D) Molecular energy decomposition for CAS/DMRG wavefunctions            
                                                                                
        E) Effective atomic orbitals:                                           
           I. Mayer, J. Phys. Chem. 100 6249 1996                               
           I. Mayer and P. Salvador, J. Chem. Phys. 130 234106 2009             
           E. Ramos-Cordoba et al., J. Chem. Phys. 138 214107 2013              
                                                                                
        F) Local spin analysis                                                  
           E. Ramos-Cordoba et al., J. Chem. Theory Comput. 8 1270-1279 2012    
           E. Ramos-Cordoba et al., Phys. Chem. Chem. Phys. 14 15291-15298 2012 
                                                                                
        G) Effective Oxidation states analysis                                  
           E. Ramos-Cordoba et al., J. Chem. Theory Comput. 11 1501-1508 2015   
                                                                                
        H) Oxidation states from localized orbitals                             
           M. Gimferrer, G. Comas-Vila, P. Salvador, Molecules 25 234 2020      
           M. Gimferrer et al., Inorg. Chem. 59 15410-15420 2020                
           M. Gimferrer et al., J. Chem. Theor. Comput. 18 309-322 2022         
                                                                                
        I) Decomposition of EDA quantities into one- and two-center IQA terms   
           M. Gimferrer et al., J. Chem. Theory Comput. 19 3469-3485 2023       
                                                                                
        J) Origin-independent decomposition of static polarizabilities          
           M. Montilla, et al., J. Chem. Theory Comput. 17, 1098-1105 2021      
                                                                                
                                                                                
      Cite this program as:                                                     
      ---------------------                                                     
        P. Salvador, E. Ramos-Cordoba, M. Montilla, L. Pujal and M. Gimferrer   
        J. Chem. Phys., 2024, 160, 172502 DOI: 10.1063/5.0206187                
                                                                                
    e-mail: psalse@gmail.com, eloy.raco@gmail.com, mgimferrer18@gmail.com       
                                                                                
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    The program has been written by using parts of the program APOST by         
    I. Mayer and A. Hamza, Budapest, 2000-2003.                                 
                                                                                
    The numerical integration utilizes the subroutines for Lebedev              
    quadrature downloaded from CCL. The appropriate reference is:               
    V.I. Lebedev, and D.N. Laikov "A quadrature formula for the sphere of the   
    131st algebraic order of accuracy" Doklady Mathematics, 59 477-481 1999.    
                                                                                
    The program makes use of libxc library when necessary, using the F90        
    interfaces provided by the authors.                                         
                   (see http://www.tddft.org/programs/libxc)                    
                                                                                
    We are extremely grateful for the possibility of using these routines!      
                                                                                
